# prose_translation = Socrates: So consider carefully, then, whether you too share this view and agree with it, and let us start our deliberation from this point: that it is never right to do wrong, nor to do wrong in return for wrong, nor, when one suffers evil, to defend oneself by doing evil in return — or do you depart from this and fail to share in this starting-point?
