# sentence_id = 299
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Or was it not fair treatment, then, toward your father — if you happened to have one — or toward a master, as it is also fair toward a master, that whatever you suffer you should also do in return, neither to answer back when spoken ill of, nor to strike back when struck, nor many other such things?
# literal_translation = Or was [it] not then toward your father on equal terms, or toward a master, as [it is] also toward a master, if you happened to have [one], so as [for you] to do in return these very things which you might suffer — neither, being spoken ill of, to answer back, nor, being struck, to strike back, nor many other such other things?
