# sentence_id = 318
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = For you would never have lived here in Athens, more than all the other Athenians, so exceptionally, unless it had suited you exceptionally; you never went out of the city to a festival, nor anywhere else at all except once to the Isthmus, nor did you ever make any other trip abroad, as other people do, nor did any desire ever take you to know another city or other laws — we and our city were enough for you.
# literal_translation = For not ever would [you] have lived in it [i.e. the city], distinctively beyond all the other Athenians, unless it had been distinctively pleasing to you; and [you] went out neither to a festival-viewing ever from the city, except once to the Isthmus, nor [to] anywhere else at any other time, unless [you were] going to go on campaign somewhere; nor did [you] ever make any other trip abroad, as the other men [do]; nor did desire [take] you [to] know of another city or of other laws, but we were sufficient for you, and our city.
