# sentence_id = 329
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = So are you breaking some other agreement, or the covenants and compacts you made with us, not under compulsion, not deceived, and not forced to decide in a short time, but over seventy years, in which it was open to you to leave, if we were not pleasing to you and those agreements seemed to you unjust?
# literal_translation = Something else, then, [are] you transgressing, or the covenants and agreements, the [ones] toward us ourselves, [that you] agreed to—not having agreed under compulsion, nor having been deceived, nor having been forced to deliberate in a short time, but in seventy years, in which it was possible for you to depart, if we were not pleasing [to you] and the agreements did not appear [to you] to be just?
