# sentence_id = 348
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = For there, no doubt, it would most likely be greatest disorder and licentiousness, and perhaps people would gladly hear about you — how you ran away from the prison ridiculously disguised in some rig, either putting on a leather jerkin or taking some other garb such as runaways are accustomed to dress themselves up in, and changing your own appearance.
# literal_translation = For there, indeed, [there would be] greatest disorder and licentiousness; and perhaps they would gladly hear of you, how ridiculously you ran away from the prison, having put on some disguise, either a leather coat having taken, or other things such as those running away are indeed accustomed to dress themselves up in, and having changed the shape, the [shape] of yourself.
