# sentence_id = 365
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = But if you go away like that, disgracefully returning wrong for wrong and harm for harm, breaking your agreements and covenants with us, and doing harm to these very people whom you ought least of all to have harmed—yourself, your friends, your country, and us—then we will be angry with you while you live, and there too our brother laws in Hades will not receive you kindly, knowing that you tried your best to destroy us as well.
# literal_translation = And if you go out thus disgracefully, having both wronged in return and done harm in return, your own agreements and covenants, those toward us, having transgressed, and having worked these evils, whom it was least necessary [to harm]—yourself, and friends, and country, and us—we will be angry at you while living, and there the laws, our brothers, those in Hades, will not receive you kindly, knowing that you tried to destroy us too, so far as lay in your part.
