# sentence_id = 367
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Socrates: Know this well, dear friend Crito—I do seem to hear these arguments just as the corybants seem to hear the flutes, and in me this very echo of these words resounds and makes it impossible for me to hear anything else.
# literal_translation = Socrates: These things, O dear friend, comrade, Crito, know well that I myself seem to hear, just as those who are corybant-raving seem to hear of the flutes, and in me this same echo of these words buzzes and makes [me] not able to hear of the others.
